; Move what a carrier holds to a new location, bringing the player along
;
; Called when an actor or object has been put at a new location (B). Sets
; MoveFlag to 1 and gives the new location to everything the carrier holds,
; and what those hold (#R$9C17). If that walk met the player (MoveFlag was
; cleared: the player is inside or carried by the carrier), the player arrives
; too: with the player as the actor (Subject 0, ActorRecord the player's record,
; TakeId = B) it runs the arrival part of the take routine (#R$8E12), then
; #R$9B02 refreshes what the player can see, and the actor is restored. The
; arrival step is skipped when the player's first location ($C12B) is 0.
; MoveFlag is 0 when the routine ends with the player carried.
; .
; A Id of the carrier (an actor or an object that holds things)
; B The new location
@label=MoveCarried
@isub=LD HL,MoveFlag
c$9BDD LD HL,$9BDC   ;
 $9BE0 LD (HL),$01   ;
 $9BE2 CALL $9C17    ; relocate the contents
 $9BE5 LD A,(HL)     ;
 $9BE6 AND A         ;
 $9BE7 RET NZ        ; the player was not among them
 $9BE8 PUSH HL       ;
 $9BE9 LD A,($C12B)  ; the player's first location
 $9BEC AND A         ;
 $9BED JR Z,$9C13    ;
 $9BEF LD A,($B6EA)  ; keep the actor
 $9BF2 PUSH AF       ;
 $9BF3 LD HL,($B70C) ; and its record
 $9BF6 PUSH HL       ;
 $9BF7 LD HL,$C11B   ; the player
 $9BFA LD ($B70C),HL ;
 $9BFD XOR A         ;
 $9BFE LD ($B6EA),A  ; Subject := player
 $9C01 LD A,B        ;
 $9C02 LD ($8D9B),A  ; TakeId := the new location
 $9C05 CALL $8E12    ; the player arrives
 $9C08 CALL $9B02    ;
 $9C0B POP HL        ;
 $9C0C LD ($B70C),HL ;
 $9C0F POP AF        ;
 $9C10 LD ($B6EA),A  ;
*$9C13 POP HL        ;
 $9C14 XOR A         ;
 $9C15 LD (HL),A     ; MoveFlag := 0
 $9C16 RET           ;
